\pard \fs24
{\plain \fs36 \i\f1\fs36 Concerning the Rite}{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1  \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20 The ministry of reconciliation, which has been committed by Christ to\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20 his Church, is exercised through the care each Christian has for others,\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20 through the common prayer of Christians assembled for public worship,\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20 and through the priesthood of the Church and its ministers declaring\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20 absolution.\par
}\pard \fs20\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20  \par
}\pard \fs20
{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20 The Reconciliation of a Penitent is available for all who desire it. It is not \softline
restricted to times of sickness. Confessions may be heard anytime and anywhere.\par
}\pard \fs20\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20  \par
}\pard \fs20
{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20 Two equivalent forms of service are provided here to meet the needs of\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20 penitents.  The absolution in these services may be pronounced only by a\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20 bishop or priest. Another Christian may be asked to hear a confession,\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20 but it must be made clear to the penitent that absolution will not be\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20 pronounced; instead, a declaration of forgiveness is provided.\par
}\pard \fs20\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20  \par
}\pard \fs20
{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20 When a confession is heard in a church building, the confessor may sit\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20 inside the altar rails or in a place set aside to give greater privacy,\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20 and the penitent kneels nearby.  If preferred, the confessor and\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20 penitent may sit face to face for a spiritual conference leading to\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20 absolution or a declaration of forgiveness.}{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20 \par
}\pard \fs20\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20  \par
}\pard \fs20
{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20 When the penitent has confessed all serious sins troubling the conscience and \softline
has given evidence of due contrition, the priest gives such counsel \par
}{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20 and encouragement as are needed and pronounces absolution. Before \par
}{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20 giving absolution, the priest may assign to the penitent a psalm, prayer, \par
}{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20 or hymn to be said, or something to be done, as a sign of penitence and \par
}{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20 act of thanksgiving.\par
}\pard \fs20\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20  \par
}\pard \fs20
{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20 The content of a confession is not normally a matter of subsequent\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20 discussion. The secrecy of a confession is morally absolute for the\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20 confessor, and must under no circumstances be broken.}{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1  \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1  \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1  \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}\column 
\pard \fs44
{\plain \fs44 \f1\fs44 The Reconciliation\par
}{\plain \fs44 \f1\fs44 of a Penitent}{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1  \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1  \par
}{\plain \fs24 \b\f1 Form One}{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f1\fs20 The Penitent begins}{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}\pard \fs24\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}\pard \fs24
{\plain \fs24 \f1 Bless me, for I have sinned.\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f1\fs20 The Priest says}{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}\pard \fs24\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}\pard \fs24
{\plain \fs24 \f1 The Lord be in your heart and upon your lips that you may\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 truly and humbly confess your sins: In the Name of the\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 Father and of the Son, and of the Holy Spirit. }{\plain \fs24 \i\f1 Amen.}{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f1\fs20 Penitent}{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}\pard \fs24\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}\pard \fs24
{\plain \fs24 \f1 I confess to Almighty God, to his Church, and to you, that\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 I have sinned by my own fault in thought, word, and deed, in\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 things done and left undone; especially__________.  For these\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 and all other sins which I cannot now remember, I am truly\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 sorry. I pray God to have mercy on me. I firmly intend\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 amendment of life, and I humbly beg forgiveness of God and\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 his Church, and ask you for counsel, direction, and absolution.\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1  \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f1\fs20 Here the Priest may offer counsel, direction, and comfort.}{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1  \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}\column 
